1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,793
A paper fill is not a win.

2
00:00:02,793 --> 00:00:09,977
Today's case study uses KO, the NYSE ticker for The Coca-Cola Company, because a broker-confirmed PAPER fill exists.

3
00:00:09,977 --> 00:00:14,366
This is an educational example, not a recommendation or live-money result.

4
00:00:14,366 --> 00:00:18,756
The position remains open, and no exit fill has been confirmed.

5
00:00:18,756 --> 00:00:25,540
The real lesson is what had to be checked before entry and what protection had to follow.

6
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:32,924
The daily research showed an aligned trend structure and positive relative strength and momentum versus a broad-market reference.

7
00:00:32,924 --> 00:00:39,077
Liquidity and spread checks were acceptable in the connected feed, while volume confirmation was weaker.

8
00:00:39,077 --> 00:00:40,307
That caveat matters.

9
00:00:40,307 --> 00:00:46,871
A setup ranking organizes evidence; it does not predict the next move or prove company profitability.

10
00:00:46,871 --> 00:00:52,203
It also does not replace a fresh quote or a completed intraday candle.

11
00:00:52,203 --> 00:00:58,808
The first time check found a mismatch between the market clock and quote timestamps, so the process paused.

12
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:01,010
A fresh comparison later aligned them.

13
00:01:01,010 --> 00:01:04,312
Only then did the system recheck completed intraday bars.

14
00:01:04,312 --> 00:01:12,751
The quote was above session VWAP, the latest completed short-interval closes were rising, and price had not moved too far from its reference.

15
00:01:12,751 --> 00:01:14,219
Partial candles were excluded.

16
00:01:14,219 --> 00:01:18,622
This is why a recheck is a safety step, not a formality.

17
00:01:18,622 --> 00:01:21,168
Position sizing was decided before execution.

18
00:01:21,168 --> 00:01:27,957
The process compared the risk budget, the maximum exposure allowed for one position, and available cash.

19
00:01:27,957 --> 00:01:30,079
The smallest permitted size won.

20
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:38,990
After the broker confirmed the actual fill, a separate native trailing stop was placed for the protected quantity and verified open.

21
00:01:38,990 --> 00:01:41,111
No take-profit target was added.

22
00:01:41,111 --> 00:01:44,506
The stop is not a guaranteed loss cap.

23
00:01:44,506 --> 00:01:46,497
What could invalidate the setup?

24
00:01:46,497 --> 00:01:54,464
A loss of the trend structure, weaker relative strength, a failed intraday reference, stale data, or a triggered protective stop.

25
00:01:54,464 --> 00:02:00,438
The process does not average down or add simply because a position moves against it.

26
00:02:00,438 --> 00:02:04,820
The position remains open and the protective stop remains in place.

27
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:08,803
No exit fill exists, so no closed-trade result is reported.

28
00:02:08,803 --> 00:02:14,856
A confirmed fill starts the management phase; it does not finish the story.

29
00:02:14,856 --> 00:02:24,168
Record the entry evidence, verify protection, monitor invalidation conditions and report the actual exit only when the broker confirms it.

30
00:02:24,168 --> 00:02:27,894
This is a paper simulation, not live-money performance.

31
00:02:27,894 --> 00:02:31,153
AMORDER: evidence first, risk always, no promises.

32
00:02:31,153 --> 00:02:36,741
Paper-trading education only; not live-money performance; not investment advice; no guaranteed returns.
